$$2800 = (v_S + 28)^2 - v_S^2$$
$$2800 = (v_S^2 + 56v_S + 784) - v_S^2$$
$$2800 = 56v_S + 784$$
$$56v_S = 2800 - 784 = 2016$$
$$v_S = \frac{2016}{56} = 36 \text{ m/min}$$

### 5. Finding D

Substitute $v_S = 36$ back into (Eq. S):
$$3600 = 36^2 + K^2 (36 + 14)^2$$
$$3600 = 1296 + K^2 (50)^2$$
$$3600 - 1296 = 2500 K^2$$
$$2304 = 2500 K^2$$
$$K^2 = \frac{2304}{2500}$$
$$K = \sqrt{\frac{2304}{2500}} = \frac{48}{50} = \frac{24}{25}$$

Recall that $K = 528/D$.
$$\frac{24}{25} = \frac{528}{D}$$
$$D = 528 \cdot \frac{25}{24}$$
Since $528 / 24 = 22$:
$$D = 22 \cdot 25 = 550$$

The distance $D$ is 550 meters.

