$k=6$: $f(6) = \omega^{18} + \omega^6 + 1 = \omega^4 + \omega^6 + 1$.

The product is $P = 3 \cdot (\omega^3 + \omega + 1) \cdot (\omega^6 + \omega^2 + 1) \cdot (\omega^2 + \omega^3 + 1) \cdot (\omega^5 + \omega^4 + 1) \cdot (\omega + \omega^5 + 1) \cdot (\omega^4 + \omega^6 + 1)$.

This looks complicated to multiply directly. We should look for a structural simplification.

Let $x = \omega^k$. We are looking at $x^3 + x + 1$.

