    The required set of remainders is $\{0, 1, r_4, r_5, 4\}$. These must be distinct.
    $r_4 \in \{0, 1, 2, 3\}$. $r_4$ cannot be 0, 1, 4. So $r_4 \in \{2, 3\}$.
    $r_5 \in \{0, 1, 2, 3, 4\}$. $r_5$ cannot be 0, 1, 4. So $r_5 \in \{2, 3\}$.

