This product is precisely the resultant of the polynomials $Q(z)$ and $R(z)$, denoted $\text{Res}(Q(z), R(z))$.

If $Q(z)$ has roots $\beta_1$ and $\beta_2$, then $\text{Res}(Q(z), R(z)) = R(\beta_1) R(\beta_2)$.

The roots of $Q(z) = z^2 + z + 1 = 0$ are the primitive cube roots of unity, $\zeta_3$ and $\zeta_3^2$.
