We use the vector relationship: $\vec{v}_{g} = \vec{v}_{w} + \vec{v}_r$, which means $\vec{v}_{w} = \vec{v}_{g} - \vec{v}_r$.

Let $C = D/2$. The path from $S$ to $P$ has a horizontal displacement of $C$ and a vertical displacement of $264$.
The path from $M$ to $P$ has a horizontal displacement of $-C$ and a vertical displacement of $264$.

